🌐 Basics of Computer Networking


📌 Introduction

A computer network is a group of connected devices that communicate with each other to share data and resources. It enables efficient communication and supports services such as email, file sharing, and internet access.

🔹 Key Features of Computer Networks

Connects multiple devices such as computers, servers, and printers

Enables data and resource sharing

Supports communication services (email, messaging)

Allows internet and network-based applications

Improves efficiency and collaboration

📘 Basic Terminologies
🔹 Network

A group of connected computers and devices that can communicate and share data.

🔹 Node

Any device that can send, receive, or forward data in a network.
Examples: Laptops, mobiles, printers, earbuds, servers.

🔹 Networking Devices

Devices that manage and support networking functions.
Examples: Routers, switches, hubs, access points.

🔹 Transmission Media

The medium through which data travels between devices.

Wired Media: Ethernet cables, Optical fibre

Wireless Media: Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, Infrared

🔹 Service Provider Networks

Networks provided by external organizations that offer internet or communication services.
Examples: Internet Service Providers (ISPs), Mobile carriers.

🛠 Basics of Computer Networks
🔹 Building Blocks

Network Node: Any device such as a modem, router, or computer that sends or receives data

Link: The medium connecting nodes (cables, wires, wireless signals)

🔹 Working of a Computer Network

Networks use protocols to send and receive data

Each device is identified using a unique IP Address

🔹 Firewall

A security tool (hardware or software) that monitors network traffic.
It allows, blocks, or drops data based on predefined rules.

🏗 Types of Computer Network Architecture
1️⃣ Client–Server Architecture

Nodes act as Clients or Servers

Server manages and controls client behavior

Common in enterprise and web applications

2️⃣ Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Architecture

No central server

Each device can act as both client and server

Simple and cost-effective for small networks

🔌 Network Devices
1️⃣ Router

Connects multiple networks (e.g., home network to internet)

Directs data packets to correct destinations

2️⃣ Switch

Connects devices within a network

Sends data only to the intended device

3️⃣ Hub

Basic networking device

Sends data to all connected devices (less efficient)

4️⃣ Bridge

Connects and filters traffic between network segments

Reduces network congestion

5️⃣ Gateway

Connects different types of networks

Translates data between different protocols

6️⃣ Access Point (AP)

Provides wireless connectivity

Extends wired networks into Wi-Fi networks

7️⃣ Modem

Converts digital data to transmission signals and vice versa

Enables internet access

8️⃣ Firewall

Monitors and controls network traffic

Prevents unauthorized access

🎯 Goals of Computer Networks

Convenience: Makes computer usage easier

Efficiency: Improves performance through resource sharing

Resource Management: Efficient CPU, memory, I/O, and storage usage

Security & Protection: Safeguards data and systems

Reliability & Fault Tolerance: Ensures smooth operation and recovery

Scalability: Supports growth in users and resources

🚀 Uses of Computer Networks

Communication: Email, chat, video conferencing

Resource Sharing: Printers, scanners, files

Remote Access: Access systems from anywhere

Collaboration: Teamwork and project sharing

E-commerce: Online shopping and secure payments

Education: Online learning, research, and collaboration
